<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sarup Singh of Jind</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1812">1812</a>–<a href="/years/1864">1864</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sarup Singh was Raja of Jind, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> princely state in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, from 1837 until his death in 1864. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-rebellion-of-1857">Indian Rebellion of 1857</a> he sent troops to support the British at the siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>, and was rewarded with additional territory and honours. He strengthened the administration of the state from its capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sangrur">Sangrur</a>.</p></div>
